WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:08.620
The Daily Body Count. Every single day: one hundred and fifty thousand people stop existing one hundred and thirty thousand

2
00:00:08.620 --> 00:00:16.180
from disease (diseases are very effective at their job). eighty thousand were preventable (you had the technology, you just

3
00:00:16.180 --> 00:00:23.320
chose not to use it). thirteen thousand seven hundred are children (which matters if you believe children should continue

4
00:00:23.320 --> 00:00:34.040
existing). That's fifty nine elevens. Every. Single. Day. After the first nine eleven, America invaded two countries and

5
00:00:34.040 --> 00:00:41.480
spent two trillion dollars. After the fifty daily nine elevens, humanity shrugs and checks Instagram.

6
00:00:42.520 --> 00:00:49.080
Every hour: six thousand two hundred and fifty deaths. Every minute: one hundred and four deaths.

7
00:00:49.960 --> 00:00:59.020
Every second: one point seven deaths. If you took everyone in a decent-sized stadium and deleted them, that's one day.

8
00:00:59.580 --> 00:01:02.700
Then do it again tomorrow. And the day after that. Forever.

9
00:01:03.580 --> 00:01:08.560
You'd run out of stadiums before you'd run out of corpses, which seems like poor urban planning.

10
00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:15.000
That's the body count. Now let's talk about the bill. The Financial Cost.

11
00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:22.120
While you read this sentence, disease just deleted twelve point six million dollars of human potential from existence.

12
00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:29.740
By the time you finish this paragraph, sixty million dollars more will evaporate into cancer treatments, heart surgeries,

13
00:01:29.940 --> 00:01:35.630
and funeral expenses. Also Dave from accounting's weird rash, but that's probably unrelated.

14
00:01:36.120 --> 00:01:43.920
Humanity hemorrhages three hundred ninety-seven point four trillion dollars annually to diseases that are basically just

15
00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:49.640
engineering problems with meat robots. That's more than the entire global economy.

16
00:01:50.320 --> 00:01:55.580
Every year. You lose more money to disease than you make doing everything else combined.

17
00:01:56.820 --> 00:02:01.720
It's like running a lemonade stand that costs more in lemons than the entire G.D.P.

18
00:02:01.900 --> 00:02:08.080
of Earth. "Wait," you say, demonstrating basic arithmetic skills, "global G.D.P.

19
00:02:08.300 --> 00:02:13.900
is only one hundred and one trillion dollars. How can we lose more than everything that exists?".

20
00:02:14.980 --> 00:02:22.420
Because economists forgot to include the dying part. For centuries, economics measured productivity without accounting for

21
00:02:22.420 --> 00:02:25.920
the people who stopped being productive on account of being dead.

22
00:02:26.800 --> 00:02:33.580
This is like calculating the cost of a plane crash without including the plane, the passengers, or the fact that they were

23
00:02:33.580 --> 00:02:39.040
going somewhere. The Actual Bill (Economist-Approved Misery Accounting).

24
00:02:40.440 --> 00:02:48.660
Here's what disease actually costs, translated from economist-speak into human language: Direct Medical Costs mean paying

25
00:02:48.980 --> 00:02:56.280
doctors to Google your symptoms in a room that costs five hundred dollars per hour, totaling eight point two trillion dollars.

26
00:02:56.880 --> 00:03:04.640
Lost Productivity means sick people make fewer spreadsheets, decreasing global PowerPoint supply, totaling six point seven

27
00:03:04.640 --> 00:03:14.440
trillion dollars. Lost Human Life, or disability-adjusted life years, or D.A.L.Y.s, means dead people contribute zero to

28
00:03:14.440 --> 00:03:21.780
the economy (economists finally noticed), totaling three hundred eighty-two point five trillion dollars.

29
00:03:22.420 --> 00:03:31.180
The TOTAL DISASTER is more money than exists on Earth, totaling three hundred ninety-seven point four trillion dollars.

30
00:03:32.200 --> 00:03:35.820
Let me explain that last one, because it's where the real horror lives.

31
00:03:36.800 --> 00:03:40.620
How to Measure Suffering Without Feeling Feelings (The D.A.L.Y.).

32
00:03:41.300 --> 00:03:47.600
disability-adjusted life years, or D.A.L.Y.s stands for "Disability-Adjusted Life Year."

33
00:03:48.620 --> 00:03:54.600
That's economist-speak for "quantifying human misery without having to look people in the eye.".

34
00:03:55.020 --> 00:04:02.430
One D.A.L.Y. One year of healthy human life, deleted. Die at 40 instead of 80?

35
00:04:02.840 --> 00:04:12.640
That's 40 D.A.L.Y.s. Spend 10 years severely depressed? That's 5 D.A.L.Y.s (economists calculated that being miserable counts

36
00:04:12.640 --> 00:04:18.880
as being half-dead, which is oddly accurate). The entire human species combined?

37
00:04:19.660 --> 00:04:31.720
2.55 BILLION D.A.L.Y.s annually. That's 2.55 billion years of human potential, dissolving annually into medical bills and

38
00:04:31.720 --> 00:04:37.700
funeral expenses. What the W.H.O. Thinks You're Worth (Less Than a Tesla).

39
00:04:39.080 --> 00:04:45.480
The World Health Organization decided one year of human life is worth one to three times G.D.P.

40
00:04:45.860 --> 00:04:49.690
per capita. They made this calculation sober, which is surprising.

41
00:04:51.020 --> 00:04:58.460
Let's use three times G.D.P. per capita. We're optimists who think humans are worth at least three years of their economic

42
00:04:58.460 --> 00:05:05.120
output. This is the most generous estimate bureaucrats could manage, and it's still less than a luxury sedan.

43
00:05:06.080 --> 00:05:13.980
The math is simple and horrifying: The value per healthy year is one hundred fifty thousand dollars (less than a Tesla,

44
00:05:14.720 --> 00:05:21.200
apparently). The total D.A.L.Y.s lost annually is two point five five billion years.

45
00:05:22.020 --> 00:05:29.120
Multiply these together: That's three hundred eighty-two point five trillion dollars of human potential.

46
00:05:29.860 --> 00:05:36.560
We flush it annually down the toilet labeled "diseases we haven't cured yet because the money went to bombs.".

47
00:05:37.800 --> 00:05:46.040
Let's Break Down This Apocalypse By Time Unit. Three hundred ninety-seven point four trillion dollars annually breaks down

48
00:05:46.040 --> 00:05:52.900
to: One point zero nine trillion dollars EVERY DAY (more than most countries make in a year).

49
00:05:53.720 --> 00:05:59.380
Forty-five billion dollars EVERY HOUR (enough to fund a mid-size cancer research institute).

50
00:06:00.840 --> 00:06:06.140
Seven hundred fifty-seven million dollars EVERY MINUTE (more than most lottery jackpots).

51
00:06:07.480 --> 00:06:17.500
Twelve point six million dollars EVERY SECOND (a new Tesla Roadster worth of human potential, gone, every second, forever).

52
00:06:18.940 --> 00:06:26.560
By the time you finish this chapter (about 10 minutes), disease will have cost humanity more than the entire Apollo moon

53
00:06:26.560 --> 00:06:31.240
program. We went to the moon for less than one chapter's worth of disease costs.

54
00:06:32.240 --> 00:06:41.420
The math is, as your children say, not mathing. What's Actually Deleting Everyone (The Greatest Hits).

55
00:06:41.640 --> 00:06:49.000
Here's what's killing people while you read about what's killing people: Heart disease causes twenty million deaths annually,

56
00:06:49.440 --> 00:06:56.340
which is fifty-four thousand eight hundred every day, meaning five hundred people will die while you're reading this chapter.

57
00:06:57.260 --> 00:07:05.440
Cancer causes ten point four million deaths annually, or twenty-eight thousand five hundred per day, and two hundred sixty

58
