Dementia causes two point six million deaths annually, or seven thousand one hundred per day, and sixty-five during this

61
00:07:26.800 --> 00:07:35.980
chapter. Diabetes causes three point four million deaths annually, which is nine thousand three hundred per day, and eighty-five

62
00:07:35.980 --> 00:07:44.560
while reading this. Kidney disease causes one point four million deaths annually, or three thousand eight hundred per day,

63
00:07:45.040 --> 00:07:53.460
and thirty-five while reading this. Tuberculosis causes one point three million deaths annually, which is three thousand

64
00:07:53.460 --> 00:08:03.200
six hundred per day, and thirty-three while reading this. In total, fifty-five million people die annually, which is one

65
00:08:03.280 --> 00:08:09.800
hundred fifty thousand per day, meaning one thousand three hundred seventy will die while you read this chapter.

66
00:08:10.520 --> 00:08:16.820
One thousand three hundred seventy humans will permanently stop existing while you read this chapter.

67
00:08:17.720 --> 00:08:20.660
That's five seven-forty-sevens crashing. Every ten minutes.

68
00:08:21.280 --> 00:08:28.160
Forever. If this happened to actual planes, you'd ground all flights within an hour and the twenty-four-hour news cycle

69
00:08:28.160 --> 00:08:35.860
would collapse from overuse. But because it's disease, you call it "natural causes" and go back to arguing about parking.

70
00:08:37.380 --> 00:08:45.900
While you're busy testing zero point zero zero zero zero zero three percent of potential cures: Ten million people annually

71
