Six hundred thousand people annually die from malaria (mosquitoes: six hundred thousand, humanity: zero).

73
00:09:00.640 --> 00:09:06.980
Ten point four million people annually die from cancer (your own cells killing you because they forgot how to die).

74
00:09:07.840 --> 00:09:14.780
Twenty million people annually die from cardiovascular disease (hearts that gave up on humanity, can't blame them).

75
00:09:15.600 --> 00:09:22.060
Each death represents: Someone's entire universe ending. A grandmother who won't meet grandchildren.

76
00:09:22.380 --> 00:09:25.600
A scientist who might have cured the thing that killed them.

77
00:09:26.100 --> 00:09:32.200
Four million dollars in lost economic value (if we're being cold about it, which economists always are).

78
00:09:32.840 --> 00:09:37.550
Infinite sadness if you're the one dying, mild inconvenience if you're not.

79
00:09:38.320 --> 00:09:43.530
Your Body Is Not Magic, It's Just Broken. Your body is a machine.

80
00:09:43.760 --> 00:09:51.520
Not mystical, not "in balance with the universe." A biological machine made of thirty-seven trillion cells.

81
00:09:52.100 --> 00:10:01.260
And like all machines, it breaks. Machines can be fixed. Every disease is just a broken part: cancer is cells with broken

82
00:10:01.260 --> 00:10:10.680
