83
00:10:11.400 --> 00:10:18.180
You don't fix them because you haven't tested ninety-nine point nine nine nine nine nine seven percent of the repair tools.

84
00:10:18.760 --> 00:10:22.340
There are one hundred sixty-six billion possible molecules.

85
00:10:23.040 --> 00:10:26.760
You've tried roughly zero point zero zero three percent of them.

86
00:10:27.300 --> 00:10:31.360
That's like trying to find your car keys by checking one pocket then giving up forever.

87
00:10:32.660 --> 00:10:40.980
What This Actually Costs. The three hundred ninety-seven point four trillion dollars "Disease Tax" is optional.

88
00:10:41.120 --> 00:10:48.080
Not optional like "you can skip it," but optional like "it's not a law of physics, just a choice humanity keeps making.".

89
00:10:48.900 --> 00:10:53.040
It's the price you pay for being too slow to fix your own broken meat robots.

90
00:10:53.740 --> 00:10:58.880
Every day you delay costs another one point zero nine trillion dollars.

91
00:10:59.480 --> 00:11:08.320
Not theoretical future money. Real human potential dissolving right now into medical bills, funeral expenses, and GoFundMe

92
00:11:08.320 --> 00:11:13.820
